From 23ae49386160079cdf5e798b3c5cc6660e089c95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Siddhartha Srivastava <siddhartha@delphai.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:29:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] jobstate: public-good pool, canary units, watcher checks
 and forced errors (build step 5)

- Council: t-of-m keyholders (Params.Council) approve actions by PROPOSE/APPROVE; actions run
  as CouncilAccount.
- Pool: council-created categories (fixed public work lists for one model, cap shares of pool
  income, curator). POOL_CLAIM opens a unit as a job whose client is the pool; verifier pay is
  escrowed from the category budget; units settled in an epoch share PoolSpendBP of the budget
  equally (the unit price), minus the treasury share. Abandoned or failed units are released.
- Canary units: CANARY_REVEAL opens a hidden canary leaf after TRACE_COMMIT; every stage is
  then opened and the first mismatch is disputed by the curator down to one operation.
- Watchers: a CHALLENGE whose claimed root equals the provider's is a check: it costs
  WatchFee (paid to the provider) instead of the bond.
- Forced errors: FE_COMMIT reserves treasury funds against H(record || salt); FE_REVEAL, once
  every decoy has ended, pays Jackpot to the catchers of each caught decoy, reimburses its
  bond, and returns the rest. Stats count settled work, checks, and caught and missed decoys.

Tests: council threshold, exact pool accounting and unit pricing, claim rules, exhaustion and
retirement, canaries and forced errors with real games on the tiny Qwen3, watcher checks, a
randomized run (pool, canaries, cheaters, decoys, watchers; decoy catch rate matches the
sampling odds), cross-language vectors for verifier/forced_errors.py. The harness now also
continues every 5th block from a gob round trip of the state.

